It includes numeric interface constants (register addresses, bit-field offsets,
and a USB-JTAG command encoding) hand-transcribed from the following upstream
projects. No source code, macro text, or comments were copied; only the numeric
facts required to interoperate, plus an independently re-expressed TAP scan
algorithm. See ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md for the full analysis and the pinned commit
(upstream.lock).

1. openocd-esp32 — https://github.com/espressif/openocd-esp32
   - src/jtag/drivers/esp_usb_jtag.c   (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright Espressif Systems)
   - src/jtag/drivers/bitq.c           (GPL-2.0-or-later)
   Ported: the esp_usb_jtag USB-JTAG command nibble layout, VEND_JTAG_SETDIV,
   CMD_FLUSH, the JTAG caps descriptor wValue, and the TAP scan model. These are
   used as uncopyrightable hardware-interface facts; attribution is provided here
   as a courtesy and to document provenance.

2. RISC-V External Debug Support specification, via openocd-esp32
   - src/target/riscv/debug_defines.h  (SPDX: BSD-2-Clause OR CC-BY-4.0)
   Auto-generated from https://github.com/riscv/riscv-debug-spec
   Ported under the BSD-2-Clause option: the RISC-V Debug Module register
   addresses and field bit-offsets. The BSD-2-Clause copyright notice and
   disclaimer apply to those constants; this NOTICE preserves the attribution.
